WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:04.970
Where I come from

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:05.980
it takes courage

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.010
to become an independent journalist.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.210
Most media outlets in Russia work under censorship

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.840
and it’s harder from year to year to speak
freely

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.560
regardless of the issues.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.830
Three months after the assassination of my
father Boris Nemtsov,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.730
a Russian opposition politician,

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:24.509
I came to Berlin to deliver a speech

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:26.609
about freedom of the press.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:29.519
And on the same day I decided to leave Russia.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:32.980
For me, it was a step towards freedom.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.040
The most direct association with Germany is
freedom

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.090
and I strongly believe that it is the necessary
precondition

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.980
for creativity and, ultimately, progress.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.640
My life in Germany started here

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.820
just 100 meters from the Brandenburg Gate

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.050
a symbol of unity that used to represent division.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.690
And I still have hope

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.480
that the current period of tensions

00:00:55.480 --> 00:01:01.750
between Russia and Europe will come to an end.

